1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,030
Good morning and thank you for coming here today.

2
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:10,474
I'd like to bring you up to date with changes in the school that

3
00:00:10,474 --> 00:00:11,640
will affect your children.

4
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:16,711
As you know, the school buildings date from various times:

5
00:00:16,711 --> 00:00:21,181
some from the 1970s, some from the last five years,

6
00:00:21,181 --> 00:00:25,390
and of course Dartfield House is over a century old.

7
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:29,583
It was commissioned by a businessman, Neville Richards,

8
00:00:29,583 --> 00:00:32,312
and intended as his family home,

9
00:00:32,312 --> 00:00:34,960
but he died before it was completed.

10
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:38,659
His heir chose to sell it to the local council,

11
00:00:38,659 --> 00:00:40,730
who turned it into offices.

12
00:00:40,730 --> 00:00:46,603
A later plan to convert it into a tourist information centre didn't come about,

13
00:00:46,603 --> 00:00:48,086
through lack of money,

14
00:00:48,086 --> 00:00:54,120
and instead it formed the nucleus of this school when it opened 40 years

15
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:54,320
ago.

16
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:59,712
The school has grown as the local population has increased,

17
00:00:59,712 --> 00:01:04,163
and I can now give you some news about the lower school site,

18
00:01:04,163 --> 00:01:07,370
which is separated from the main site by a road.

19
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:12,450
Planning permission has been granted for development of both sites.

20
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:18,245
The lower school will move to new buildings that will be constructed on the

21
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:19,010
main site.

22
00:01:19,010 --> 00:01:24,430
Developers will construct houses on the existing lower school site.

23
00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:29,830
Work on the new school buildings should start within the next few months.

24
00:01:29,830 --> 00:01:36,770
A more imminent change concerns the catering facilities and the canteen.

25
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:42,722
The canteen is always very busy throughout the lunch period – in fact it's

26
00:01:42,722 --> 00:01:44,185
often full to capacity,

27
00:01:44,185 --> 00:01:48,534
because a lot of our pupils like the food that's on offer there.

28
00:01:48,534 --> 00:01:51,590
But there's only one serving point,

29
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:56,530
so most pupils have to wait a considerable time to be served.

30
00:01:56,530 --> 00:02:03,688
This is obviously unsatisfactory, as they may have hardly finished their lunch before afternoon

31
00:02:03,688 --> 00:02:04,710
lessons start.

32
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:08,175
So we've had a new Food Hall built,

33
00:02:08,175 --> 00:02:11,640
and this will come into use next week.

34
00:02:11,640 --> 00:02:13,349
It'll have several serving areas,

35
00:02:13,349 --> 00:02:17,108
and I'll give you more details about those in a minute,

36
00:02:17,108 --> 00:02:21,893
but one thing we ask you to do, to help in the smooth running

37
00:02:21,893 --> 00:02:26,678
of the Food Hall, is to discuss with your children each morning which type

38
00:02:26,678 --> 00:02:29,412
of food they want to eat that day,

39
00:02:29,412 --> 00:02:32,830
so they can go straight to the relevant serving point.

40
00:02:32,830 --> 00:02:37,815
There won't be any junk food – everything on offer will be healthy –

41
00:02:37,815 --> 00:02:43,632
and there's no change to the current system of paying for lunches by topping

42
00:02:43,632 --> 00:02:46,540
up your child's electronic payment card online.

43
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:52,000
You may be wondering what will happen to the old canteen.

44
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,602
We'll still have tables and chairs in there,

45
00:02:54,602 --> 00:02:59,155
and pupils can eat food from the Food Hall or lunch they've brought from

46
00:02:59,155 --> 00:02:59,480
home.

47
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:04,880
Eventually we may use part of the canteen for storage,

48
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:11,360
but first we'll see how many pupils go in there at lunchtime.

49
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:15,848
OK, back to the serving points in the Food Hall,

50
00:03:15,848 --> 00:03:22,132
which will all have side dishes, desserts and drinks on sale, as well as

51
00:03:22,132 --> 00:03:23,030
main courses.

52
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:27,500
One serving point we call World Adventures.

53
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:34,038
This will serve a different country's cuisine each day, maybe Chinese one day

54
00:03:34,038 --> 00:03:36,050
and Lebanese the next.

55
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:39,940
The menus will be planned for a week at a time,

56
00:03:39,940 --> 00:03:44,890
so pupils will know what's going to be available the whole of that week.

57
00:03:44,890 --> 00:03:52,230
Street Life is also international, with food from three particular cultures.

58
00:03:52,230 --> 00:03:55,059
We'll ask pupils to make suggestions,

59
00:03:55,059 --> 00:04:00,246
so perhaps sometimes there'll be food from Thailand, Ethiopia and Mexico,

60
00:04:00,246 --> 00:04:06,847
and then one of them will be replaced by Jamaican food for a week

61
00:04:06,847 --> 00:04:07,790
or two.

62
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:14,750
The Speedy Italian serving point will cater particularly for the many pupils who don't eat meat

63
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:15,620
or fish:

64
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:21,710
they can be sure that all the food served there is suitable for them.

65
00:04:21,710 --> 00:04:23,891
There'll be plenty of variety,

66
00:04:23,891 --> 00:04:27,380
so they shouldn't get bored with the food.

67
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:27,430
OK,

68
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:31,240
that's all on the new Food Hall.

69
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:34,650
Now after-school lessons.

70
00:04:34,650 --> 00:04:40,711
These are very popular with pupils, particularly swimming – in fact there's a waiting

71
00:04:40,711 --> 00:04:42,110
list for lessons.

72
00:04:42,110 --> 00:04:43,943
Cycling is another favourite,

73
00:04:43,943 --> 00:04:50,359
and I'm delighted that dozens of pupils make use of the chance to learn

74
00:04:50,359 --> 00:04:52,650
to ride in off-road conditions.

75
00:04:52,650 --> 00:04:56,800
It means that more and more cycle to and from school every day.

76
00:04:56,800 --> 00:05:00,447
As you know, we have a well-equipped performance centre,

77
00:05:00,447 --> 00:05:04,500
and we're going to start drama classes in there, too.

78
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:07,866
Pupils will be able to join in just for fun

79
00:05:07,866 --> 00:05:12,241
or work up to taking part in a play – we hope to put

80
00:05:12,241 --> 00:05:14,260
on at least one a year.

81
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:18,362
We already teach a number of pupils to use the sound

82
00:05:18,362 --> 00:05:20,600
and lighting systems in the centre.

83
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:25,280
And a former pupil has given a magnificent grand piano to the school,

84
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:30,320
so a few pupils will be able to learn at the school instead of

85
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:35,000
going to the local college, as many of them do at the moment.
